% ============================================================================
% ocean-zones.query.adj — worked recall over the ocean-zones library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what position is this
% zone in, by depth?" (direct) or "which zone comes first/second/etc.?"
% (reverse) — it states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries.
% ============================================================================

import "ocean-zones.adj"

? ocean_zone(twilight_zone, $N)   % expect 2 (direct: what position is the twilight zone?)
? ocean_zone($Z, 1)               % expect sunlight_zone (reverse: which zone comes first?)
? ocean_zone(abyssal_zone, $N)    % expect abstain -- a real deeper zone the source names, but not one of the three tabled here
